[finding.0.142]
revision = "ca388c494"
command = "cargo test --locked --manifest-path agent/Cargo.toml -p layerx-client --test sequencer"
exit_code = 0
log_path = "logs/0.142-verify-1.log"
observed_and_assumption = "verify passed (13 passed, 0 failed). Gaps: none for 11021.2 scope. Note for 6.6.5: the node serves transactionsRoot as the Comet DataHash (rpc/block.go:479), a merkle over Cosmos tx bytes, so EVM raw transactions re-encoded from the full transaction objects cannot be checked against it directly; the raw bytes are rebuilt by RLP from the object fields (types 0-4) because the node's RPCTransaction has no raw field, and the tx hash is not re-derived because layerx-client has no keccak dependency (Cargo.toml outside touches). Unrelated: agent/Cargo.lock on origin/main is stale: layerx-interop-gateway lists sha3 in its manifest but not in the lock, so every --locked cargo command in agent/ fails 'lock file needs to be updated'; the one-line lock refresh happened as a build side effect in this worktree and is left uncommitted (not owned). clippy -p layerx-client --all-targets is red on prior pedantic findings in layerx-types (program_lifecycle.rs:74,86), layerx-crypto (disclosure/native.rs:473, disclosure/program.rs:186, disclosure.rs:1269) and layerx-client (client.rs, resolver.rs, evidence/arbiter_admission.rs); with --no-deps --cap-lints warn the two owned files show no findings (logs/0.142-clippy-5.log)."

